   "id": "fomc-minutes-hikes",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Fed officials see further rate rises as likely after October hold",
   "when": "Wed 18 Nov · 14:00 ET",
   "what": "Minutes of the 27-28 October meeting show a 10-2 vote to keep the policy range at 3.75% to 4%. Lisa Cook and Beth Hammack wanted a 25 basis point rise. Almost all participants judged more increases would likely be needed. A couple said a larger move could be considered if inflation data disappoint. September PCE inflation was 3.6%, core 3.1%. The S&P 500 closed down 0.23% and the 10-year yield eased 4 bp to 5.07%.",
   "why": "Higher policy rates weigh on equity valuations and support the dollar. Your S&P 500 funds are priced as of 13 and 16 November, so this morning the dashboard does not yet show the S&P 500 drop of about 3.2% since 13 November.",
