   "id": "nvidia-results-korea",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Nvidia's strong quarter lifts Seoul chip names; CEO seat is vacant",
   "when": "Tue 17 Nov · after US close",
   "what": "Nvidia reported fiscal third-quarter revenue of $115.8 billion, up 103% from a year earlier, with data centre sales of $107.6 billion. It guided to $130 billion plus or minus 3% for the next quarter, assuming no China data centre compute sales. Colette Kress is interim CEO while a successor is sought. KOSPI rose 1.99% to 5,067.44, ending a three-day slide. Samsung Electronics gained 2.31% and SK hynix 4.19%.",
